From stable+bounces-352401-greg=kroah.com@vger.kernel.org Wed Oct  7 12:41:54 2026
From: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Date: Wed,  7 Oct 2026 05:07:10 -0400
Subject: iio: adc: adi-axi-adc: Initialize state mutex
To: stable@vger.kernel.org
Cc: Janani Sunil <janani.sunil@analog.com>, Stable@vger.kernel.org, Jonathan Cameron <jonathan.cameron@oss.qualcomm.com>, Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Message-ID: <20261007090651.2021301-2-sashal@kernel.org>

From: Janani Sunil <janani.sunil@analog.com>

[ Upstream commit 549b71ce050637dd32678371ad76c445a2f8c9aa ]

The AXI ADC register access paths serialize transactions with st->lock,
but probe does not initialize it. Initialize the mutex before registering
the backend.

Fixes: 7ecb8ee5c93b ("iio: adc: adi-axi-adc: support digital interface calibration")
Signed-off-by: Janani Sunil <janani.sunil@analog.com>
Cc: <Stable@vger.kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Cameron <jonathan.cameron@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
---
 drivers/iio/adc/adi-axi-adc.c |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/iio/adc/adi-axi-adc.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/adi-axi-adc.c
@@ -715,6 +715,10 @@ static int adi_axi_adc_probe(struct plat
 	if (!st)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
+	ret = devm_mutex_init(dev, &st->lock);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	base = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0);
 	if (IS_ERR(base))
 		return PTR_ERR(base);
